IMPORT prelude

-- Limitation Act 1981 (NT) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- Built-in date functions only (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR), not the
-- daydate library. The Act counts its periods in whole years ("a limitation period of 3 years from the date on which the
-- cause of action first accrues", s 12(1)), months ("within 6 months after the date of the service of the notice",
-- s 39(1); "12 months", s 44(3)(b)(i)) and days (56 days, s 44AA); the s 36 suspension adds plain days.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Not an official version of the Limitation Act 1981 (NT). Copyright in Northern Territory legislation is
-- owned by the Northern Territory. Quoted under the Northern Territory copyright policy of 8 October 1996; see
-- SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Limitation Act 1981`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is after` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of` `the first day` `and` `the second day` MEANS
    IF `the first day` `is after` `the second day`
    THEN `the first day`
    ELSE `the second day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earlier of` `the first day` `and` `the second day` MEANS
    IF `the first day` `is before` `the second day`
    THEN `the first day`
    ELSE `the second day`

-- The number of days in a month of a year.
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in month` m `of` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- The same day and month n years later (n may be negative); 29 February falls on 28 February in a year that has none
-- (fork F1 in NOTES.md). With the day of the event excluded, a period of n years "from" day D ends at the end of this
-- day, so it is the last day on which the action is maintainable.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the anniversary` n `years after` `the start` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (min (DATE_DAY `the start`) (`the days in month` (DATE_MONTH `the start`) `of` `the target year`)) (DATE_MONTH `the start`) `the target year`
    WHERE
        `the target year` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the start` PLUS n

-- The same day n months later, for 0 to 12 months; a day the later month lacks falls on its last day (fork F1).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `months after` `the start` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (min (DATE_DAY `the start`) (`the days in month` `the target month` `of` `the target year`)) `the target month` `the target year`
    WHERE
        `the month count` MEANS DATE_MONTH `the start` PLUS n
        `the target month` MEANS
            IF `the month count` GREATER THAN 12
            THEN `the month count` MINUS 12
            ELSE `the month count`
        `the target year` MEANS
            IF `the month count` GREATER THAN 12
            THEN DATE_YEAR `the start` PLUS 1
            ELSE DATE_YEAR `the start`

-- The day a person born on a day reaches an age: the birthday (fork F2 in NOTES.md).
GIVEN `the age` IS A NUMBER, `the birth day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day of reaching age` `the age` `for birth on` `the birth day` MEANS `the anniversary` `the age` `years after` `the birth day`
